tival Black Lives Matter panel, Obioma saw it fit to make his intervention into the debate ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... I, a great new African writer is asking these questions in a spare yet extraordinary novel about this bloody stain on human history.\\\"\\n\\n–Chigozie Obioma (The New York Times Book Review)\\n\\nFinalists:\\n\\nPeter Cameron, What Happens at Night (Catapult)\\n\\nAkwaeke Emezi, The Death of Vivek Oji (Riverhead)\\n\\nDanielle ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma, in The Orchestra of Minorities does the same. You shall notice in my next novel, The Wanderers [to be published in April/May], that I delve into this a little deeper also, to depict the notion of the absurdity of the human condition, which though popularized ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f155604d6f39f65969be7813e02d29e86b14d9377a2e8e81808f1ef0b387a886\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a8b1c88e0b32ddf4cad77240334085c82df546e6109cfd7d1c0ffdf387028a2f\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma Wikipedia\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Lucy Ellmann | Ducks, Newburyport | Galley Beggar | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Chigozie Obioma | An Orchestra of Minorities | Little, Brown | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Salman Rushdie | Quichotte ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... As Erigha (2019, 2021) shows, \\\"racial valuations\\\" operate through an interaction between creators' racial identities and the genre categories their works are slotted into. We show that in the construction of the category of postcolonial literature through the Booker Prize (Anand and Jones 2008), non-white authors end ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 1997, the decision to award Arundhati Roy's The God of Small Things proved controversial. Carmen Callil, chair of the previous year's Booker judges, called it an \\\"execrable\\\" book and said on television that it should not even have been on the shortlist. Booker Prize chairman ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her 2019 translation of Krishna Sobti's A Gujarat Here, a Gujarat There was awarded the Modern Language Association's Aldo and Jeanne Scaglione Translation Prize.\\n\\nIn speaking to the jury's rationale, the panel's chair, Wynne is quoted, saying, \\\"This has been an exceptionally strong shortlist ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize 2023 Shortlist\\n\\nAt London Book Fair: Insights Into Translation Buyers\\n\\nAs the news of the International Booker Prize shortlist was announced to the public amid the raucous noise and crush of simultaneously programmed events at London Book Fair's opening today (April 17), the ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2023/04/london-book-fair-the-bookers-new-data-on-translation-buyers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... She is the author of the prize-winning Regeneration trilogy. The last book in the series, The Ghost Road, won the Booker Prize in 1995. Her latest novel, The Silence of the Girls, was shortlisted for the 2019 Women's Prize for Fiction.\\n\\nBarker has been on Writers ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book was the joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize.\\n\\nNonfiction\\n\\nIn 2008, Atwood published Payback: Debt and the Shadow Side of Wealth, a collection of five lectures delivered as part of the Massey Lectures from October 12 to November 1, 2008. The book was released in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"8371ebc85e31ad72f4a00a822c9ae73c2b3e4732b4f12175c00e889319c8fab1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"c120e0e3f2844415a0dcb1a2c4e8b19a0d605f46500f198a62aec377c41a8298\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"An Orchestra of Minorities 2019 Booker shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_93a3b28734df4a628782545a"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. Let me reconsider the structure carefully:\n\n- Award created in 2000s → International Booker Prize (established 2005)\n- Book A: contender for this award, translated into 25+ languages, published in the 2010s\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won the award\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in city where author of Book A grew up\n\nKey candidate: Chigozie Obioma's \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. But wait — that's the Booker Prize, not the International Booker Prize. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, the question says \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention.\" So Book A is a contender for the award, and Book B won that same award. Let me check the International Booker Prize winners in the 2010s and look for the connection. Let me search for the Wikipedia page on the International Booker Prize.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize Wikipedia\", \"Booker International Prize 2016 2017 2018 2019 winner\", \"Man Booker International Prize Wikipedia\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_9ca1d3cbffbd405dab54632a","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma biography born Akure grew up\", \"Chigozie Obioma Wikipedia\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities 2019 Booker shortlist\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_746be3a170ff4b2b9e784232","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":true,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_Catton\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Powers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl,_Woman,_Other\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"rea